  <h2>Part 1: The Color Extractor</h2>

  <p>
    The extractor analyzes an image and identifies the colors that define it. Each color appears as a tile with its HEX and RGB value; one click on the copy icon puts the code on the clipboard. Markers on the image show where each color comes from.
  </p>

  <h3>What You Can Adjust</h3>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Image source:</strong> upload your own photo or click one of the sample images to try the tool right away.</li>
    <li><strong>Number of colors:</strong> how many colors are extracted, for example 5 for a compact palette.</li>
    <li><strong>Format:</strong> output color values as HEX or RGB, depending on what your design tool expects.</li>
    <li><strong>Image editing:</strong> zoom, brightness, contrast, saturation and hue can be changed with sliders. The extraction responds to them, so you can get a stronger or more muted palette from the same photo.</li>
    <li><strong>Effects:</strong> blur smooths details and yields calmer blended colors, grayscale reduces the image to brightness values.</li>
    <li><strong>Export:</strong> download the edited image as PNG in a selectable size — and the extracted palette in nine formats, from a plain HEX list to design tokens.</li>
  </ul>

